<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Volksraad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Volksraad (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> for 'people's council') was the elected legislature of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> republics of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in the 19th century, including the Natalia Republic, the Orange Free State and the South African Republic. Its members were chosen by enfranchised white <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a>, and it made laws, controlled finances and chose or supervised the executive.</p></div>
